=== How to use ===
1. Add the plugin to a declarative agent through its actions array and package the files with an app manifest.
2. Add every domain that the card uses, for example the host of the webUrl link in Action.OpenUrl or image URLs, to validDomains in the app manifest. Otherwise Teams warns about untrusted content and images are not rendered.
3. Test with an account that has no open opportunities. An empty array can render a blank card unless you guard it, for example with a TextBlock that uses $when and length($root).
4. Preview the card JSON with sample data in the Adaptive Card designer before you paste it into static_template.
5. If different result types need different layouts, add template_selector to properties and return the templates with the API response; static_template stays as the fallback.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Pointing data_path at the wrong level, so the card receives the whole response object instead of one opportunity.
- Using card features that the target host does not support; prefer single-column layouts that also work in narrow Copilot panes.
- Exposing write operations in a plugin that is meant to be read-only. The description_for_model promises read-only behavior, so the API scope should enforce it.
- Returning huge payloads: large responses waste context and make answers slower.
- Forgetting that findAccounts must run first; spell the call order out in description_for_model.

An approval plugin for managers that reads pending expense requests and records decisions. It focuses on the controls you want around state-changing actions: a custom confirmation card per write function (capabilities.confirmation), security_info with ResourceStateUpdate, and a reasoning-state instruction that forces the model to list requests before it decides on one. Non-GET operations always prompt the user in Copilot, and the confirmation title and body replace the generic text (Microsoft Learn: confirmation prompts for MCP and API plugins). Manifest schema v2.4.

=== File: ai-plugin.json ===
Comment: for states, an array in instructions augments the built-in prompt while a plain string would replace it. isNonConsequential defaults to false; do not set it to true for approvals.
{
 "$schema": "https://developer.microsoft.com/json-schemas/copilot/plugin/v2.4/schema.json",
 "schema_version": "v2.4",
 "name_for_human": "Expense Approvals",
 "namespace": "ContosoApprovals",
 "description_for_human": "Review and decide on expense requests that wait for your approval.",
 "description_for_model": "Use this plugin when a manager asks which expense requests wait for approval or wants to approve or reject one. Only the signed-in approver's own pending requests are available. Never approve or reject a request unless the user has clearly named the request and the decision in the current conversation turn.",
 "contact_email": "finance-apps@contoso.example",
 "functions": [
  {
   "name": "listPendingApprovals",
   "description": "Lists expense requests that are waiting for the signed-in user's decision.",
   "capabilities": {
    "security_info": {
     "data_handling": [
      "GetPrivateData"
     ]
    }
   },
   "states": {
    "reasoning": {
     "description": "Resolve which request the user means.",
     "instructions": [
      "Always call listPendingApprovals before approveRequest or rejectRequest so that the request ID comes from a function result."
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "approveRequest",
   "description": "Approves one pending expense request.",
   "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
     "requestId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ID of the pending request."
     },
     "comment": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional comment for the requester."
     }
    },
    "required": [
     "requestId"
    ]
   },
   "capabilities": {
    "confirmation": {
     "type": "AdaptiveCard",
     "title": "Approve expense request",
     "body": "Approve this expense request? The requester is notified immediately.",
     "isNonConsequential": false
    },
    "security_info": {
     "data_handling": [
      "ResourceStateUpdate"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "rejectRequest",
   "description": "Rejects one pending expense request. A reason is mandatory.",
   "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
     "requestId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ID of the pending request."
     },
     "reason": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Why the request is rejected."
     }
    },
    "required": [
     "requestId",
     "reason"
    ]
   },
   "capabilities": {
    "confirmation": {
     "type": "AdaptiveCard",
     "title": "Reject expense request",
     "body": "Reject this expense request with the reason you gave?"
    },
    "security_info": {
     "data_handling": [
      "ResourceStateUpdate"
     ]
    }
   }
  }
 ],
 "runtimes": [
  {
   "type": "OpenApi",
   "auth": {
    "type": "OAuthPluginVault",
    "reference_id": "REPLACE_WITH_AUTH_CONFIG_ID"
   },
   "spec": {
    "url": "approvals-openapi.json",
    "progress_style": "ShowUsageWithInput"
   }
  }
 ]
}

=== File: approvals-openapi.json (shortened) ===
Comment: the decision endpoints are POST operations, so Copilot asks for confirmation. Keep one operation per decision to make the confirmation text precise.
